The complete predecessor-plus-CP32 contract matrix then ran independently
against each clean source/build side in the same networkless, empty-sysfs
containment. Both matrices reached all three final CP32 pass lines and exited
zero. A convenience wrapper attempted to summarize both completed logs using
rg, which was intentionally absent from the minimal container, and returned
127 after the matrices had finished. This was a summary-command issue only;
the retained logs are complete and their terminal pass lines were confirmed
outside the container.

